      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately the error code for the `error` callback is context dependent and is a uint16_t primitive to cover all possible errors in the various address spaces.\n\nThere are at least 3 address spaces and they (mostly) map to the l2cap result in the l2cap packet.\n```\ntL2CAP_CONN\ntL2CAP_LE_RESULT\ntL2CAP_CFG_RESULT\n```\n\nThis mostly works because the source and sink are context aware; further, the underlying codes may overlap correctly.  For example, success is always zero.\n\nI agree this needs fixing, but this requires an API update across all profiles to handle properly.",
